        "number": 3,
        "title": "CSS From Zero",
        "subtitle": "The Box Model, Flexbox, CSS Grid, custom properties, responsive design, and animations",
        "readingTime": "28 min",
        "videoLesson": {
          "title": "Modern CSS Architecture, Flexbox, Grid & Responsive Layouts",
          "channel": "freeCodeCamp.org",
          "duration": "06:18:00",
          "videoId": "1Rs2ND1ryYc",
          "watchUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Rs2ND1ryYc",
          "embedUrl": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/1Rs2ND1ryYc",
          "url": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/1Rs2ND1ryYc",
          "alternativeSource": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS",
          "sourceName": "MDN Web Docs — Modern CSS Layout",
          "badge": "Verified Reference Video"
        },
        "summary": "Transform raw markup into stunning, responsive layouts. Master the CSS Box Model, Flexbox alignment, two-dimensional CSS Grid, media queries, CSS variables, and modern visual effects.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Explain the CSS Box Model (content, padding, border, margin) and configure `box-sizing: border-box`.\n2. Master one-dimensional layouts using Flexbox (axes, alignment, distribution, wrapping, and gaps).\n3. Architect two-dimensional grid systems using CSS Grid (`grid-template-columns`, `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...))`).\n4. Build responsive, mobile-first websites using media queries and fluid typography units (`rem`, `ch`, `clamp()`).\n5. Utilize CSS Custom Properties (variables) to implement scalable design systems and dark mode themes.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Universal CSS Reset & The Box Model\n\nEvery element in HTML is a rectangular box:\n\n```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n|                          MARGIN                           |\n|   +---------------------------------------------------+   |\n|   |                      BORDER                       |   |\n|   |   +-------------------------------------------+   |   |\n|   |   |                  PADDING                  |   |   |\n|   |   |   +-----------------------------------+   |   |   |\n|   |   |   |              CONTENT              |   |   |   |\n|   |   |   |        (Width x Height)           |   |   |   |\n|   |   |   +-----------------------------------+   |   |   |\n|   |   +-------------------------------------------+   |   |\n|   +---------------------------------------------------+   |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n#### The Golden Standard Reset:\n```css\n/* Universal Border-Box Reset */\n*, *::before, *::after {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\n:root {\n  --color-primary: #0284c7;\n  --color-accent: #10b981;\n  --color-bg: #0f172a;\n  --color-text: #f8fafc;\n  --font-sans: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Flexbox: 1-Dimensional Alignment Mastery\n\nFlexbox organizes elements along a single axis (row or column):\n\n```css\n.nav-container {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  justify-content: space-between; /* Horizontal spacing */\n  align-items: center;            /* Vertical centering */\n  gap: 1.5rem;                    /* Spacing between items */\n}\n```\n\n| Property | Values | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `display` | `flex`, `inline-flex` | Activates flex formatting context |\n| `justify-content` | `flex-start`, `center`, `space-between`, `space-around` | Aligns items along main axis |\n| `align-items` | `stretch`, `center`, `flex-start`, `flex-end` | Aligns items along cross axis |\n| `flex-wrap` | `nowrap`, `wrap` | Allows items to break into new lines |\n\n---\n\n### 3. CSS Grid: 2-Dimensional Layout Powerhouse\n\nCSS Grid handles both rows and columns simultaneously. The responsive auto-fit pattern is industry standard:\n\n```css\n.course-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));\n  gap: 2rem;\n  padding: 2rem;\n}\n\n.course-card {\n  background: #1e293b;\n  border-radius: 0.75rem;\n  padding: 1.5rem;\n  border: 1px solid #334155;\n  transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;\n}\n\n.course-card:hover {\n  transform: translateY(-4px);\n  border-color: var(--color-accent);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Mobile-First Responsive Design\n\nAlways style for mobile smartphones first, then use `min-width` media queries for larger screens:\n\n```css\n/* 1. Mobile Default (1 Column) */\n.layout {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 1rem;\n}\n\n/* 2. Tablet & Desktop (2 Columns) */\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .layout {\n    flex-direction: row;\n  }\n  .sidebar {\n    width: 280px;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n  }\n  .content {\n    flex-grow: 1;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Activities & Practical Exercises\n\n#### Exercise 1: Responsive 3-Card Grid Challenge\nBuild a responsive pricing section containing three cards (Starter, Pro, Enterprise). Use CSS Grid with `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))`, style the cards with rounded corners, padding, subtle box-shadows, and a hover scale effect.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Module Knowledge Quiz\n\n**Question 1:** What problem does `box-sizing: border-box` solve in CSS?\n- A) It makes all text uppercase\n- B) It includes padding and borders within the element's specified width and height, preventing layout breakage *(Correct)*\n- C) It removes all margins from images\n- D) It activates hardware GPU acceleration\n*Explanation: With border-box, an element with width: 300px and 20px padding remains 300px wide instead of expanding to 340px.*\n\n**Question 2:** Which CSS Grid property creates a responsive multi-column grid without requiring media queries?\n- A) `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));` *(Correct)*\n- B) `grid-columns: 3 auto;`\n- C) `display: table-cell;`\n- D) `flex: 1 1 100%;`\n*Explanation: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)) dynamically fills available width with columns that never shrink below 250px.*\n\n---\n\n### 7. Module Summary & Key Takeaways\n- Use `box-sizing: border-box` in your CSS reset to maintain predictable box calculations.\n- Use Flexbox for 1D component layouts (navbars, button groups) and CSS Grid for 2D page architecture.\n- Follow mobile-first responsive principles using `min-width` media queries and `rem` units.",
        "challenge": {
          "type": "quiz",
          "title": "Module 3 Checkpoint: CSS Layouts",
          "question": "In CSS Flexbox, which property distributes flex items with equal space between them across the main axis?",
          "options": [
            "align-items: space-between",
            "justify-content: space-between",
            "flex-direction: space-between",
            "text-align: justify"
          ],
          "correctAnswer": 1,
          "explanation": "justify-content: space-between distributes items evenly across the main axis, placing the first item at the start and the last item at the end."
        }
