        "summary": "Implement production-grade identity and access management. Master salted bcrypt password hashing, stateless JSON Web Tokens (JWT), token expiration, Role-Based Access Control middleware, and secure password reset flows.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Distinguish between **Authentication** (verifying identity) and **Authorization** (verifying permissions).\n2. Hash and salt passwords securely with `bcryptjs` using appropriate work factors (cost >= 10).\n3. Generate, sign, verify, and decode stateless **JSON Web Tokens (JWT)** with standard cryptographic algorithms (HMAC-SHA256).\n4. Author reusable Express authentication and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) middleware.\n5. Design secure account recovery and password reset workflows using time-limited cryptographic tokens.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Password Security & Salting with Bcrypt\n\nNever store plaintext passwords or use fast cryptographic hashes (like plain MD5 or SHA-256) for passwords. Fast hashes allow attackers to calculate billions of guesses per second using rainbow tables and GPUs.\n\n**Bcrypt** uses an adaptive key derivation function with an adjustable **work factor (cost)** and a unique cryptographic **salt** for every password:\n\n```javascript\nconst bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');\n\n// Hash password on user registration\nasync function hashPassword(plainPassword) {\n  const SALT_ROUNDS = 12; // 12 rounds = ~250ms computation time on modern server CPU\n  return await bcrypt.hash(plainPassword, SALT_ROUNDS);\n}\n\n// Compare password on user login (constant-time comparison prevents timing attacks)\nasync function verifyPassword(plainPassword, storedHash) {\n  return await bcrypt.compare(plainPassword, storedHash);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. JSON Web Tokens (JWT) Architecture\n\nA JWT is a compact, URL-safe token that securely transmits claims between the client and server. It consists of three parts separated by dots: `header.payload.signature`.\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                              JWT ANATOMY                                |\n|                                                                         |\n|  1. HEADER (Algorithm & Token Type)                                     |\n|     { \"alg\": \"HS256\", \"typ\": \"JWT\" }                                    |\n|                                                                         |\n|  2. PAYLOAD (User Claims & Expiration - Base64 encoded)                 |\n|     { \"userId\": \"usr_101\", \"role\": \"learner\", \"exp\": 1799999999 }       |\n|                                                                         |\n|  3. SIGNATURE (Cryptographic Verification)                              |\n|     HMACSHA256(base64(header) + \".\" + base64(payload), JWT_SECRET)      |\n|                                                                         |\n|  Result: eyJhbGciOi... . eyJ1c2VySWQiOi... . 5K9aXz_w8mPq12...          |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Implementing JWT Authentication in Express\n\n#### A. Generating the Token on Login\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\n\nfunction generateAuthToken(user) {\n  const payload = {\n    userId: user.id,\n    email: user.email,\n    role: user.role\n  };\n\n  // Sign with secret key and set 7-day expiration\n  return jwt.sign(payload, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '7d' });\n}\n```\n\n#### B. Verification Middleware (`middleware/auth.js`)\n```javascript\nconst jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\n\nconst authenticateToken = (req, res, next) => {\n  const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];\n  // Expect format: \"Bearer <token>\"\n  const token = authHeader && authHeader.split(' ')[1];\n\n  if (!token) {\n    return res.status(401).json({ success: false, error: 'Access token required. Please sign in.' });\n  }\n\n  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, decodedUser) => {\n    if (err) {\n      return res.status(403).json({ success: false, error: 'Invalid or expired token.' });\n    }\n    req.user = decodedUser; // Attach authenticated user payload to request!\n    next();\n  });\n};\n\nmodule.exports = { authenticateToken };\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Middleware\n\nRBAC ensures that administrative endpoints (such as updating course prices or viewing revenue audits) are accessible only to authorized roles:\n\n```javascript\n// middleware/authorizeRoles.js\nconst requireRoles = (...allowedRoles) => {\n  return (req, res, next) => {\n    if (!req.user || !allowedRoles.includes(req.user.role)) {\n      return res.status(403).json({\n        success: false,\n        error: `Forbidden: Access requires one of the following roles: ${allowedRoles.join(', ')}`\n      });\n    }\n    next();\n  };\n};\n\n// Usage on admin routes:\n// router.post('/courses', authenticateToken, requireRoles('admin', 'instructor'), createCourse);\n// router.get('/admin/revenue', authenticateToken, requireRoles('admin'), getRevenueReport);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Practical Hands-On Exercise\n\nImplement a secure password reset token generation and verification module:\n\n```javascript\n// services/passwordResetService.js\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\nconst DB = require('../data/db');\n\nfunction createPasswordResetToken(userId) {\n  // Generate random 32-byte hex token\n  const resetToken = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');\n\n  // Hash token before storing in database (never store raw reset tokens in DB!)\n  const hashedToken = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(resetToken).digest('hex');\n  const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 15 * 60 * 1000); // 15 minutes validity\n\n  DB.savePasswordReset({ userId, hashedToken, expiresAt });\n\n  // Return unhashed token to be emailed to user\n  return resetToken;\n}\n\nfunction verifyResetToken(userId, rawToken) {\n  const expectedHash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(rawToken).digest('hex');\n  const record = DB.getPasswordReset(userId);\n\n  if (!record || record.hashedToken !== expectedHash) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid reset token');\n  }\n  if (new Date() > new Date(record.expiresAt)) {\n    throw new Error('Reset token has expired');\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Module Summary & Key Takeaways\n- Never store plaintext passwords; always use `bcrypt` with a salt round factor of at least 10–12.\n- JWTs provide stateless authentication by verifying cryptographic signatures with `JWT_SECRET`.\n- Attach verified user payloads to `req.user` in authentication middleware.\n- Enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) on sensitive endpoints before executing business logic.",
