        "summary": "Bring everything together to graduate as a job-ready backend engineer. Architect, test, and deploy an end-to-end production API service featuring PostgreSQL persistence, secure JWT authentication, RBAC, payment webhooks, OpenAPI/Swagger documentation, and live cloud deployment.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Architect an end-to-end production backend service from requirements to deployment.\n2. Author interactive API documentation using **OpenAPI 3.0 / Swagger UI**.\n3. Implement a complete feature set: Authentication, Relational Database CRUD, Role-Based Access Control, and Payments.\n4. Deploy a live backend service to a production cloud platform (Render, Railway, or AWS).\n5. Prepare for junior backend engineering technical interviews, system design questions, and code reviews.\n6. Claim your official **Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Backend Development**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Capstone Production Project Blueprint\n\nYour capstone project proves to employers and clients that you can build, secure, and maintain enterprise software.\n\n```\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  CAPSTONE BACKEND SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE                    |\n|                                                                          |\n|  [ Client Web / Mobile / Postman ]                                       |\n|                |                                                         |\n|                v                                                         |\n|  [ Cloud Load Balancer & HTTPS SSL (Cloudflare / Render) ]               |\n|                |                                                         |\n|                v                                                         |\n|  [ Express.js Production API Service (Node.js 20) ]                      |\n|    ├── Security: Helmet, CORS, Express-Rate-Limit                        |\n|    ├── Auth: JWT verification & Bcrypt password hashing                  |\n|    ├── Validation: Express middleware request schema validation          |\n|    ├── Documentation: Swagger UI (/api/docs)                             |\n|    └── Business Services: Courses, Payments, Certificates, Email        |\n|                |                                                         |\n|         +------+------+                                                  |\n|         v             v                                                  |\n|  [ PostgreSQL DB ]  [ External Services ]                                |\n|  - Users            - Safaricom Daraja STK Push                          |\n|  - Enrollments      - SMTP Transactional Email                           |\n|  - Payments         - Cloud Storage (Avatars / Assets)                   |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Interactive Documentation with OpenAPI / Swagger\n\nA professional backend is self-documenting. Swagger allows frontend teams and API consumers to test endpoints interactively:\n\n```javascript\n// swagger.js\nconst swaggerJsdoc = require('swagger-jsdoc');\nconst swaggerUi = require('swagger-ui-express');\n\nconst options = {\n  definition: {\n    openapi: '3.0.0',\n    info: {\n      title: 'FAHMRISE Learning Platform API',\n      version: '1.0.0',\n      description: 'Production REST API for courses, payments, and certificates'\n    },\n    servers: [\n      { url: 'https://api.fahmrise.com', description: 'Production Server' },\n      { url: 'http://localhost:5000', description: 'Local Development' }\n    ]\n  },\n  apis: ['./src/routes/*.js']\n};\n\nconst specs = swaggerJsdoc(options);\n\nfunction setupSwagger(app) {\n  app.use('/api/docs', swaggerUi.serve, swaggerUi.setup(specs));\n}\n\nmodule.exports = setupSwagger;\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Backend Technical Interview Preparation\n\n#### A. Core Concepts Commonly Asked in Backend Interviews:\n- **SQL vs NoSQL**: When to choose ACID relational tables (financial records, user accounts) vs flexible documents.\n- **Database Indexing**: How B-Trees accelerate lookups from $O(N)$ table scans to $O(log N)$ seeks.\n- **Connection Pooling**: Why servers pool open database connections rather than creating new TCP connections per request.\n- **Stateless vs Stateful Auth**: Tradeoffs between server-side Redis sessions vs stateless JWT tokens.\n- **Idempotency**: Why payment APIs must support idempotency keys so network retries never double-charge customers.\n\n#### B. The STAR Method for Behavioral Interviews:\n- **Situation**: Describe the project and context.\n- **Task**: Explain your specific backend engineering responsibility.\n- **Action**: Detail the technical decisions, schema designs, or optimizations you implemented.\n- **Result**: Quantify the impact (e.g. \"Reduced API latency by 60% and successfully processed over 1,000 concurrent transactions with zero duplicate records\").\n\n---\n\n### 4. Capstone Project Submission & Graduation Checklist\n\nTo complete the course and claim your certificate:\n1. Complete all 10 module checkpoint quizzes with a passing grade of 70% or higher.\n2. Build and deploy your production REST API project to the cloud (Render, Railway, or AWS).\n3. Connect your project to a live PostgreSQL database and configure continuous deployment with GitHub.\n4. Include interactive Swagger documentation at `/api/docs`.\n5. Claim your **Official Verified FAHMRISE Certificate of Completion in Backend Development**!\n\n---\n\n### 5. Module Summary & Key Takeaways\n- You have completed the comprehensive roadmap from server fundamentals to production cloud engineering.\n- You have mastered Node.js, Express, SQL database modeling, JWT authentication, RBAC, backend security, testing, and Docker deployment.\n- **Understand. Learn. Rise.** Take your skills forward and engineer the future of the web!",
