        "summary": "Understand how elite commercial data analysts operate in modern companies. Master stakeholder discovery, translate vague operational complaints into precise quantitative questions, and navigate the 6-stage analytics project lifecycle.",
        "content": "### Learning Objectives\nBy the end of this module, you will be able to:\n1. Navigate the 6 distinct stages of the **Commercial Analytics Lifecycle**: Discovery -> Data Scoping -> ETL & Modeling -> Analysis & Validation -> Storytelling & Delivery -> Impact Tracking.\n2. Conduct effective **Stakeholder Discovery Interviews** with department heads to uncover root business problems.\n3. Transform vague complaints (e.g. \"Sales are down in Western Kenya\") into testable quantitative hypotheses.\n4. Distinguish between **Actionable Business Metrics** (drive decisions) and **Vanity Metrics** (look impressive but lead to no action).\n5. Create an **Analytics Project Charter** scoping deliverables, data sources, assumptions, and deadlines.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The 6-Stage Commercial Analytics Lifecycle\n\nAmateur analysts jump straight into writing code or building charts. Professional analysts follow a disciplined end-to-end framework:\n\n```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                      THE 6-STAGE DATA ANALYTICS LIFECYCLE                     |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                               |\n|  [ 1. Discovery & Problem Framing ]                                           |\n|  Understand the core business objective and decision to be made               |\n|                         |                                                     |\n|                         v                                                     |\n|  [ 2. Data Sourcing & Scoping ]                                               |\n|  Identify tables, databases, APIs, quality risks, and schema definitions      |\n|                         |                                                     |\n|                         v                                                     |\n|  [ 3. Cleansing & Data Modeling ]                                             |\n|  Sanitize dirty records, join relational keys, build Star Schema / pipelines  |\n|                         |                                                     |\n|                         v                                                     |\n|  [ 4. Exploratory & Statistical Analysis ]                                    |\n|  Test hypotheses, compute metrics, identify anomalies and cohort drivers      |\n|                         |                                                     |\n|                         v                                                     |\n|  [ 5. Executive Storytelling & Dashboard Delivery ]                           |\n|  Translate technical outputs into clear visual dashboards & strategic memos   |\n|                         |                                                     |\n|                         v                                                     |\n|  [ 6. Decision Implementation & Impact Tracking ]                             |\n|  Monitor if recommendations improved revenue, margin, or operational SLA     |\n|                                                                               |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Summary & Best Practices\n- Never accept a vague request like \"build me a dashboard\". Ask: \"What specific decision will you make based on this data?\"\n- Focus exclusively on metrics that tie directly to revenue, gross margin, customer acquisition cost (CAC), or retention.",
