        "content": "\n# Module 2: Purification & Preparation (Taharah & Wudu)\n\nNo prayer is accepted without purification. The Prophet ﷺ said:\n> *«لاَ تُقْبَلُ صَلاَةٌ بِغَيْرِ طُهُورٍ»*  \n> *\"No prayer is accepted without purification.\"* (Sahih Muslim 224).\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is Taharah?\n\nTaharah encompasses two dimensions:\n1. **Physical Cleanliness (*Taharat al-Khabath*)**: Removing physical impurities (*Najasah*—such as urine, feces, blood) from one's body, clothing, and prayer area.\n2. **Ritual Cleanliness (*Taharat al-Hadath*)**: Lifting the state of minor ritual impurity through **Wudu** or major ritual impurity through **Ghusl**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Step-by-Step Practical Guide to Wudu (Ablution)\n\nAllah outlined the foundational elements of Wudu in the Qur'an:\n> ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا قُمْتُمْ إِلَى الصَّلَاةِ فَاغْسِلُوا وُجُوهَكُمْ وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ إِلَى الْمَرَافِقِ وَامْسَحُوا بِرُءُوسِكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ إِلَى الْكَعْبَيْنِ﴾  \n> *\"O you who have believed, when you rise to [perform] prayer, wash your faces and your forearms to the elbows and wipe over your heads and wash your feet to the ankles.\"*  \n> — **Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6)**\n\n### The Complete Sunnah Wudu Method:\n\n1. **Intention (*Niyyah*)**: Form the sincere intention in your heart to perform Wudu for the sake of Allah.\n2. **Bismillah**: Say *«بِسْمِ اللَّهِ»* (*\"In the Name of Allah\"*).\n3. **Wash Hands (3 times)**: Thoroughly wash both hands up to the wrists, rubbing between the fingers.\n4. **Rinse Mouth (*Madmadah*) (3 times)**: Take water into the mouth with the right hand, swish, and expel it.\n5. **Rinse Nose (*Istinshaq & Istinthar*) (3 times)**: Sniff water gently into the nostrils with the right hand, then blow it out using the left hand.\n6. **Wash Face (3 times)**: Wash the entire face from the hairline to the chin, and from earlobe to earlobe.\n7. **Wash Arms to Elbows (3 times)**: Wash the right arm from fingertips including the elbow 3 times, then the left arm identically.\n8. **Wipe Head & Ears (Once)**: Wet both hands and wipe backward from front hairline to the nape of the neck, then bring hands back to the front. Immediately wipe the inside of the ears with the index fingers and the outside with the thumbs.\n9. **Wash Feet to Ankles (3 times)**: Wash the right foot thoroughly up to and including the ankle bone, washing between toes, 3 times. Repeat for the left foot.\n10. **Concluding Supplication**:\n    > *«أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لاَ شَرِيكَ لَهُ، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهُ وَرَسُولُهُ، اللَّهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِي مِنَ التَّوَّابِينَ وَاجْعَلْنِي مِنَ الْمُتَطَهِّرِينَ»*  \n    > *\"I bear witness that none has the right to be worshiped but Allah alone, without partner; and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O Allah, make me among those who constantly repent and make me among those who purify themselves.\"* (Sahih Muslim 234, Jami' at-Tirmidhi 55).\n\n---\n\n## 3. What Nullifies Wudu (*Nawaqid al-Wudu*)?\n\nWudu remains valid until broken by one of the following:\n1. Any discharge from the private parts (urine, stool, gas, prostatic fluid / *Madhi*).\n2. Deep sleep where a person loses awareness of their surroundings.\n3. Complete loss of consciousness (fainting, intoxication, anesthesia).\n4. Direct skin-to-skin touching of private parts with the palm with desire (according to several scholars).\n\n*Note: Minor bleeding from a small cut, vomiting, or passing doubts does not break Wudu unless one is certain of an actual nullifier.*\n\n---\n\n## 4. Essentials of Ghusl and Tayammum\n\n* **Ghusl (Major Ritual Bath)**: Required after marital intimacy, ejaculation/wet dream, or the completion of menses (*Hayd*) and post-natal bleeding (*Nifas*). It involves intention, washing off impurity, Wudu, and washing the entire body with water from head to toe.\n* **Tayammum (Dry Purification)**: A merciful alternative when water is unavailable or medically harmful to use. It involves striking clean earth/sand once with palms, wiping the face, and wiping the back of the hands (Surah Al-Ma'idah 5:6).\n      ",
