        "content": "\n# Module 3: Rights and Manners in Relationships: Parents, Family & Neighbours\n\nIslamic manners begin at home. The truest test of character is how you treat those closest to you.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Birr al-Walidayn (Devotion to Parents)\n\nAllah placed honoring parents immediately after the command to worship Him alone:\n> ﴿وَقَضَىٰ رَبُّكَ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا إِيَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ إِحْسَانًا ۚ إِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِندَكَ الْكِبَرَ أَحَدُهُمَا أَوْ كِلَاهُمَا فَلَا تَقُل لَّهُمَا أُفٍّ وَلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا وَقُل لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِيمًا﴾  \n> *\"And your Lord has decreed that you not worship except Him, and to parents, good treatment. Whether one or both of them reach old age with you, say not to them [so much as], 'uff,' and do not repel them but speak to them a noble word.\"*  \n> — **Surah Al-Isra (17:23)**\n\n### Practical Pillars of Birr al-Walidayn:\n* **Utmost Gentleness**: Never raise your voice, scowl, or express annoyance (*\"Uff\"*).\n* **Obedience in Goodness**: Obey them in all matters that do not disobey Allah.\n* **Continuous Du'a**: Praying for their mercy in life and after death:\n  > *«رَّبِّ ارْحَمْهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيَانِي صَغِيرًا»* (*\"My Lord, have mercy upon them as they brought me up when I was small\"* — Surah Al-Isra 17:24).\n* **The Special Status of Mothers**: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: *\"Who among people is most deserving of my good companionship?\"* He replied: *«أُمُّكَ»* (*\"Your mother\"*). The man asked: *\"Then who?\"* He said: *«أُمُّكَ»* (*\"Your mother\"*). The man asked: *\"Then who?\"* He said: *«أُمُّكَ»* (*\"Your mother\"*). The man asked: *\"Then who?\"* He said: *«ثُمَّ أَبُوكَ»* (*\"Then your father\"* — Sahih al-Bukhari 5971, Sahih Muslim 2548).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Silat ar-Rahim (Maintaining Family Ties)\n\nUpholding kinship ties brings direct divine blessings in this life and the next:\n* The Prophet ﷺ said:\n  > *«مَنْ سَرَّهُ أَنْ يُبْسَطَ لَهُ فِي رِزْقِهِ، وَأَنْ يُنْسَأَ لَهُ فِي أَثَرِهِ، فَلْيَصِلْ رَحِمَهُ»*  \n  > *\"Whoever loves that his provision be expanded and his lifespan prolonged, let him maintain his kinship ties.\"* (Sahih al-Bukhari 5986, Sahih Muslim 2557).\n* **The True Meaning of Upholding Ties**: The Prophet ﷺ clarified that maintaining ties is not merely visiting relatives who visit you; the true upholder of ties is **the one who reconciles with relatives when they cut him off** (Sahih al-Bukhari 5991).\n\n---\n\n## 3. The Rights of Neighbours\n\nThe Archangel Jibreel emphasized the rights of the neighbour so intensely that the Prophet ﷺ remarked:\n> *«مَا زَالَ جِبْرِيلُ يُوصِينِي بِالْجَارِ حَتَّى ظَنَنْتُ أَنَّهُ سَيُوَرِّثُهُ»*  \n> *\"Jibreel continued to advise me concerning the neighbour until I thought he would grant him a share of inheritance.\"* (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014, Sahih Muslim 2624).\n\n### Three Categories of Neighbours:\n1. **The Muslim Kin Neighbour**: Has 3 rights (right of Islam, right of kinship, right of neighbour).\n2. **The Muslim Neighbour**: Has 2 rights (right of Islam and right of neighbour).\n3. **The Non-Muslim Neighbour**: Has 1 right (the inviolable right of good neighbourly conduct, assistance, gifts, and safety from harm).\n      ",
