        "content": "Unlike English, Arabic has three numbers: Singular (Mufrad = 1), Dual (Muthanna = 2, adds -aan or -ayn), and Plural (Jam' = 3+, sound masculine -oon, sound feminine -aat, or broken plurals).\n\n### Learning Objectives\n* Form dual and sound plural nouns from singular forms.\n\n### Key Concepts\n* Dual: Kitab (1 book) ➔ Kitabaan (2 books).\n* Sound Masculine Plural: Muslim ➔ Muslimoon / Muslimeen.\n* Sound Feminine Plural: Muslimah ➔ Muslimaat.\n* Broken Plurals: Kitab ➔ Kutub, Qalam ➔ Aqlam.\n\n### Examples & Applications\n* **كِتَابٌ (1) ➔ كِتَابَانِ (2) ➔ كُتُبٌ (3+)** (Book ➔ Two books ➔ Books) — Number progression"
