        "content": "# Chapter 2: Core Vocabulary, Numbers & Everyday Objects\n\nVocabulary is the currency of communication. In this chapter, we develop a high-frequency foundational lexicon.\n\n---\n\n## 1. High-Frequency Lexical Categories\n\n### A. Days, Months & Time\n- **Days:** Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday (*pronounced WENZ-day*), Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.\n- **Time Markers:** Yesterday, Today, Tomorrow, Morning, Afternoon, Evening, Night.\n\n### B. Numbers in Context\n- **Cardinal (Quantities):** One, two, ten, twenty, one hundred, one thousand.\n- **Ordinal (Dates & Sequences):** First (1st), Second (2nd), Third (3rd), Fourteenth (14th).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Professional & Academic High-Frequency Words\n\n| Word | Part of Speech | Common Collocation | Example Sentence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Achieve** | Verb | *achieve a goal / success* | We worked hard to achieve our target. |\n| **Effective** | Adjective | *effective method / communication* | Clear speaking is an effective tool. |\n| **Develop** | Verb | *develop skills / strategies* | You will develop strong language skills. |\n| **Resource** | Noun | *valuable resources / time* | Books and videos are great resources. |",
