        "content": "# Chapter 3: Greetings, Introductions & Social Expressions\n\nFirst impressions are shaped by how you open and navigate a conversation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Formal vs. Informal Greetings\n\n### Formal Contexts (Workplace, Academics, Official Services)\n- **Greeting:** *\"Good morning / afternoon / evening.\"*\n- **Introduction:** *\"Allow me to introduce myself. My name is [Name].\"*\n- **Response:** *\"Pleased to meet you.\"* / *\"It is an honour to make your acquaintance.\"*\n\n### Informal Contexts (Peers, Friends, Family)\n- **Greeting:** *\"Hi there!\"* / *\"Hey, how are you doing?\"* / *\"How's everything?\"*\n- **Response:** *\"I'm doing great, thanks! How about you?\"*\n\n---\n\n## 2. Navigating Small Talk & Polite Clarifications\n\nWhen you do not catch what someone said:\n- ✅ **Polite:** *\"Could you please repeat that?\"* / *\"Pardon me?\"* / *\"Sorry, I didn't quite catch that.\"*\n- ❌ **Avoid:** *\"What?!\"* (sounds abrupt or confrontational).",
