        "transcript": "In Chapter 4, we examine English grammar mechanics. English is primarily a Subject-Verb-Object (SVO) language. We explore how to formulate positive statements, negative sentences using auxiliary verbs ('do not', 'does not', 'did not'), and questions using inversion or question words (Who, What, Where, When, Why, How). We also review the core tenses: Present Simple, Present Continuous, Past Simple, and Future with 'will' and 'going to'.",
