        "content": "# Chapter 4: Sentence Building & Core Grammar Foundations\n\nGrammar is the framework that allows you to express thoughts with clarity and precision.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Core Sentence Blueprint (S-V-O)\n\nEnglish sentences follow a strict word order:\n1. **Subject (Who/What):** *The teacher*\n2. **Verb (Action/State):** *explains*\n3. **Object (Receiver):** *the lesson.*\n\n```\n[Subject: Aisha] + [Verb: studies] + [Object: international languages] + [Time: every morning].\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Essential Tenses Quick Reference\n\n| Tense | Structure | Use Case | Example |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Present Simple** | Subject + Verb(s) | Habits & facts | *He works in technology.* |\n| **Present Continuous** | Subject + am/is/are + V-ing | Actions happening now | *They are studying grammar.* |\n| **Past Simple** | Subject + Verb-ed (or irregular) | Completed past actions | *We completed the assignment.* |\n| **Future (will / going to)** | Subject + will + V / is going to + V | Future plans & predictions | *I will travel next month.* |",
