        "content": "# Chapter 3: French Greetings & Polite Social Expressions\n\nFrench culture places a profound value on courteous greetings and formal respect.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Greetings by Time of Day & Setting\n\n| Setting | French Expression | English Meaning | Usage Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Daytime (Formal & General)** | *Bonjour* | Good morning / Hello | Used all day until evening |\n| **Evening (Formal & General)** | *Bonsoir* | Good evening | Used from late afternoon onwards |\n| **Casual (Friends & Peers)** | *Salut* | Hi / Bye | Informal only |\n| **Departing (General)** | *Au revoir* | Goodbye | Standard farewell |\n| **Departing (Casual)** | *À bientôt* | See you soon | Friendly farewell |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Introducing Yourself\n- **Name:** *\"Je m'appelle [Nom].\"* (My name is...)\n- **Asking Name (Formal):** *\"Comment vous appelez-vous ?\"*\n- **Asking Name (Casual):** *\"Comment tu t'appelles ?\"*\n- **Pleasure to meet you:** *\"Enchanté\"* (m) / *\"Enchantée\"* (f).",
