          "The vowel 'E' is exemplified in words like 'meza' and 'ndege' (words like 'mwalimu' contain only a, i, u).",
          "Syllabic 'M' and 'N': In words like 'm-tu', 'm-ji', and 'n-chi', the initial consonant forms its own syllable and takes the penultimate stress.",
          "Stress rule: In virtually every Kiswahili word, stress falls predictably on the penultimate (second-to-last) syllable.",
          "Official status: Kiswahili is an official language of Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda, Rwanda, EAC, AU, and SADC."
