        "content": "# Chapter 2: Core Swahili Vocabulary, Family & Numbers\n\nExpanding your active Kiswahili word bank with essential daily nouns, numbers, and calendar terms.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Numbers in Kiswahili\n\n- **1–10:** moja (1), mbili (2), tatu (3), nne (4), tano (5), sita (6), saba (7), nane (8), tisa (9), kumi (10).\n- **Tens:** ishirini (20), thelathini (30), arobaini (40), hamsini (50), sitini (60), sabini (70), themanini (80), tisini (90), mia moja (100).\n- **Example:** 25 = *ishirini na tano*; 150 = *mia moja na hamsini*.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Days of the Week & The Swahili Calendar\n\nIn Swahili culture, the calendar week is numbered from **Saturday** (Juma + Mosi = 1st day):\n1. **Jumamosi** = Saturday (Day 1)\n2. **Jumapili** = Sunday (Day 2)\n3. **Jumatatu** = Monday (Day 3)\n4. **Jumanne** = Tuesday (Day 4)\n5. **Jumatano** = Wednesday (Day 5)\n6. **Alhamisi** = Thursday (from Arabic Al-Khamis)\n7. **Ijumaa** = Friday (Day of gathering / Jumu'ah)",
