        "content": "# Chapter 5: Swahili Listening Comprehension & Spoken Nuance\n\nTuning your auditory comprehension to native East African speech patterns.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Core Question Words for Listening\n\nWhen listening to native speakers, identifying the question word clarifies what information is being requested:\n- **Wapi?** = Where? (*Unakaa wapi?* = Where do you live?)\n- **Nani?** = Who? (*Yule ni nani?* = Who is that?)\n- **Nini?** = What? (*Unataka nini?* = What do you want?)\n- **Lini?** = When? (*Mkutano utaanza lini?* = When will the meeting start?)\n- **Kwa nini?** = Why? (*Kwa nini unajifunza Kiswahili?* = Why are you learning Swahili?)\n- **Gharama / Bei gani?** = How much? (*Hii ni bei gani?* = What price is this?)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Timeless Swahili Proverbs (Methali)\n1. **\"Haba na haba, hujaza kibaba.\"**  \n   *Little by little fills the measure.* (Great accomplishments come from steady small efforts).\n2. **\"Elimu ni mwanga.\"**  \n   *Education is light.*",
