        "transcript": "In this capstone chapter, we bring all previous skills together into practical real-world dialogues. In a Japanese café or restaurant, waitstaff welcome you with 'Irasshaimase!' (Welcome!). Order items with '[Item] o kudasai' (Please give me...). When shopping, ask 'Kore o misete kudasai' (Please show me this) or 'Kore o kudasai' (I'll take this). When paying at the cash register, say 'Kaikei o onegaishimasu' (The bill, please). You will also review essential communication strategies to ask native speakers to speak more slowly ('Mou sukoshi yukkuri hanashite kudasai') or repeat ('Mou ichido onegaishimasu').",
