        "transcript": "Somali (Af-Soomaali) is a major East African language spoken by over 25 million people across Somalia, Somaliland, Djibouti, eastern Ethiopia (Somali Region), northeastern Kenya, and a dynamic global diaspora. Belonging to the Cushitic branch of the Afroasiatic language family, Somali has an exceptionally rich poetic and oral tradition. In 1972, the official standardized Somali Latin script (Far Soomaali) was adopted, created by linguist Shire Jama Ahmed. It uses standard Latin letters without special diacritics, using combinations like 'DH', 'KH', and letters 'X' and 'C' to represent distinctive phonetic sounds.",
