        "content": "# Chapter 1: Introduction to the Somali Language\n\nWelcome to **Somali Language Learning (Barashada Af-Soomaaliga)** on FAHMRISE!\n\n---\n\n## About the Somali Language\n\nSomali (*Af-Soomaali*) is one of the most vibrant and poetic languages of Africa. It is the official language of Somalia and Somaliland, a national language in Djibouti, and widely spoken across Eastern Ethiopia and Northeastern Kenya.\n\n---\n\n## The Standard Latin Alphabet (Far Soomaali)\n\nIn October 1972, the official written script for Somali was established based on the Latin alphabet created by **Shire Jama Ahmed** (*Shire Jaamac Axmed*).\n\nKey features of the script:\n- It uses standard Latin keyboard characters without accents or foreign diacritics.\n- The letters **X** and **C** represent specific pharyngeal sounds (unvoiced pharyngeal fricative and voiced pharyngeal fricative).\n- The letter **Q** represents a voiced uvular stop.\n- Digraph **DH** represents a retroflex voiced stop, and **KH** represents a voiceless uvular fricative.",
