        "content": "# Chapter 4: Introducing Yourself & Family\n\nLearn how to talk about yourself and your family (*Qoyska*) in Somali.\n\n---\n\n## Self-Introduction Formula (Isbarasho)\n\n1. **Magacaygu waa [Magacaaga]** — My name is [Your Name]\n2. **Waxaan ahay arday / macallin** — I am a student / teacher\n3. **Waxaan ka imid [Waddanka]** — I come from [Country]\n4. **Waxaan ku noolahay [Magaalada]** — I live in [City]\n5. **Barasho wanaagsan!** — Nice to meet you!\n\n---\n\n## Family Vocabulary (Qoyska)\n\n| Somali Word | Meaning | With 'My' (Possessive) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Hooyo** | Mother | **Hooyaday / Hooyadayda** (My mother) |\n| **Aabbe** | Father | **Aabbahay / Aabbahayga** (My father) |\n| **Walaal** | Sibling | **Walaalkay** (My brother) / **Walaashay** (My sister) |\n| **Wiil** | Boy / Son | **Wiilkayga** (My son) |\n| **Gabar** | Girl / Daughter | **Gabadhayda** (My daughter) |\n| **Awoowe** | Grandfather | **Awoowahay** (My grandfather) |\n| **Ayeeyo** | Grandmother | **Ayeeyaday** (My grandmother) |",
