        "transcript": "Asking questions in Somali is structured and expressive. Yes/No questions are formed by placing the interrogative marker 'Miyaa?' at the end of the sentence or 'Ma' before the verb: 'Ma hadashaa Af-Soomaali?' (Do you speak Somali?) or 'Af-Soomaali ma taqaanaa?'. For specific inquiries, use interrogative words: Maxaa (What), Xaggee (Where), Goorma (When), Yaa (Who), Sidee (How), Waayo / Maxay tahay sababtu (Why), and Imisa (How much / How many). To answer affirmatively, say 'Haa' (Yes); for negative responses, say 'Maya' (No).",
