        "content": "# Chapter 8: Asking & Answering Simple Questions\n\nFormulating questions (*Su'aalaha*) is the bridge to natural conversation in Somali.\n\n---\n\n## Question Words (Erayada Su'aalaha)\n\n| Somali Question Word | English Meaning | Example Sentence | Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Maxaa** | What | **Maxaad samaynaysaa?** | What are you doing? |\n| **Xaggee** | Where | **Xaggee baad tagaysaa?** | Where are you going? |\n| **Goorma** | When | **Goorma ayaan kulamaynaa?** | When are we meeting? |\n| **Yaa** | Who | **Yaa la hadlayaa?** | Who is speaking? |\n| **Sidee** | How | **Sidee ku tagtay?** | How did you get there? |\n| **Imisa** | How much / How many | **Kani waa imisa?** | How much is this? |\n| **Waayo** | Why | **Waayo ma aadan imaan?** | Why didn't you come? |\n\n---\n\n## Yes / No Questions with 'Ma' & 'Miyaa'\n\n- **Adigu arday ma tahay?** (Are you a student?) $\\rightarrow$ **Haa, waxaan ahay arday** (Yes, I am a student).\n- **Biyo ma haysaa?** (Do you have water?) $\\rightarrow$ **Haa, waan hayaa** (Yes, I have) / **Maya, ma hayo** (No, I don't have).",
