        "topic": "Why We Never Trust Client Prices in E-commerce",
        "explanation": "A malicious user can open Chrome DevTools and modify a product price from $50 to $0.01 in the JavaScript state before clicking checkout. Always validate each product ID against your database on the server, sum the prices server-side, and calculate tax/discounts securely."
